# Keep build contexts small & deterministic.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
.venv
.venv-*
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.git
.github
.orchestrator
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.vscode
.claude
docs_archive
ai-activity-log.jsonl
ai-task-archive
archive
*.zip
*.log

# ODP-RELEASE-WORKFLOW-DISPATCH-PARSER-001: Runtime Release stages its receipts
# under `.odp_data/release/` inside the checkout, and the build job writes the
# environment-binding receipt before `docker build`. Those receipts carry a
# `checked_at` timestamp, so leaving them in the context would give every re-run
# of the same release SHA a different image digest -- and a Supervisor lease is
# bound to the `manifest_digest` derived from those digests. `.odp_data/` is the
# runtime data tree in general: none of it belongs in an image.
.odp_data
